  "body": "## Bug Report: Program Fails to Open on macOS\n\n**System Information**  \n- **Mac Model:** MacBook Pro with Apple M1 Max  \n- **GPU Cores:** 32-core GPU  \n- **Memory:** 64GB RAM  \n- **OS Version:** macOS 15.3.1 (German locale)\n\n**Tested Versions**  \n- **ART 1.25.2 (macOS, ARM dmg)**\n- **ART 1.25.2 (macOS, x64 dmg)**\n\n**Issue Description**  \n- After granting necessary permissions (System Preferences → Security & Privacy → Allow Anyway), the application appears to launch but never fully opens.  \n- When starting via Terminal, the program provides no verbose output or error messages, making it difficult to diagnose the cause of the failure.\n\n**Steps to Reproduce**  \n1. Download and install the DMG file (either ARM or x64) on macOS 15.3.1.  \n2. Attempt to open the application.  \n3. Observe that macOS initially blocks the app.  \n4. Allow the app in **Security & Privacy**.  \n5. Reopen the application.  \n\n**Observed Behavior**  \n- The app icon bounces or indicates an attempt to launch, but it never fully opens.  \n- No console output is generated when run via Terminal.\n\n**Expected Behavior**  \n- The application should launch successfully and display its main interface or any expected splash screen.  \n\n**Additional Information**  \n- No crash logs or error messages are generated.  \n- Reinstalling or re-downloading does not resolve the issue.  ",
